    {
      "objection": "Biane already proves Kronecker tensor products become Plancherel.",
      "resolution": "That is a limit-shape statement for one decomposition. Fine labels can retain Theta(sqrt(n)) entropy inside the common limit shape.",
      "resolved": true
    },
    {
      "objection": "Asymptotic freeness of Jucys--Murphy elements directly applies.",
      "resolution": "The located theorem concerns outer products in S_(2n); even fixed-degree same-n freeness would still require projector-resolution control.",
      "resolved": true
    },
    {
      "objection": "One exact real-valued moment can encode every partition.",
      "resolution": "The relevant class-sum eigenvalues are integers with polynomial range at fixed moved support, so their joint range is explicitly bounded.",
      "resolved": true
    },
    {
      "objection": "Support-three features distinguish almost every partition at the small n accessible to exact computation.",
      "resolution": "This finite injectivity is transient: two integer coordinates have only polynomial joint range, whereas p(n)=exp(Theta(sqrt(n))).",
      "resolved": true
    },
    {
      "objection": "Large unresolved entropy proves natural Racah MI survives.",
      "resolution": "It does not. It only proves that coarse-feature independence cannot upper-bound the hidden conditional dependence.",
      "resolved": true
    }
  ],
